    ReadingText(id: "en-read-annas-week", languageID: "en", title: "Anna's week", level: "A1", topic: "routine", unitID: "en-foundations-u3",
        text: "Anna works in a bookshop from Tuesday to Saturday. On Mondays she doesn't work — she cleans her flat in the morning and plays tennis with her sister in the afternoon. She always gets up at seven and walks to work; the bookshop opens at nine. In the evening she cooks, but on Thursdays she eats with her parents. On Sundays the bookshop is closed, and Anna likes to sleep late, read in the park and call her grandmother. Her grandmother always asks the same question: 'Do you eat enough fruit, Anna?' And Anna always says yes.",
